 ```
 
+### Configuration for Kubelet Stats Scraping
+
+Enable `presets.kubeletStats` to scrape `https://${env:K8S_NODE_NAME}:10250/metrics`
+on every node with the standard Prometheus receiver. This opt-in preset requires
+`mode: daemonset` and a Kubernetes node with an accessible kubelet. It uses the
+service-account bearer token, skips TLS certificate verification, and grants
+`get` access to `nodes/metrics`.
+
+```yaml
+mode: daemonset
+presets:
+  kubeletStats:
+    enabled: true
+    scrapeInterval: 30s
+```
+
+The only preset options are `enabled` (default `false`) and `scrapeInterval`
+(default `30s`). Customize `config.receivers.prometheus/kubelet_stats` for other
+scrape settings; user config takes precedence. This collects all kubelet metrics
+without discovery or filtering. `kubeletMetrics` instead collects `/stats/summary`;
+`kubeletPrometheusMetrics` offers curated metrics and semantic convention mapping.
+Enable only one preset for the kubelet `/metrics` endpoint to avoid duplicate scrapes.
+
 ### Configuration for Retrieving Kubelet Prometheus Metrics
 
 The collector can be configured to scrape the kubelet's own Prometheus endpoint (`/metrics`) on the local node. This covers kubelet health metrics such as running pods and containers, PLEG and runtime operation latencies, evictions, certificate TTLs, and volume stats. It complements `kubeletMetrics` (`/stats/summary`) and `kubernetesExtraMetrics` (`/metrics/cadvisor`).
